# 📈 Visualizations

## 📊 Platform Engagement Ranking

A horizontal bar chart compares engagement across major social media platforms, making it easy to identify the highest-performing channels.


## 😊 Sentiment Distribution

A donut chart illustrates the distribution of audience sentiment across five categories:

- Happy
- Angry
- Confused
- Excited
- Sad

This visualization provides a quick overview of public perception and audience reactions.


## 📅 Year-over-Year Platform Performance

Clustered column charts compare platform performance across **2024** and **2025**, highlighting growth and performance changes over time.


## 📈 Daily Engagement Trend

A line chart tracks engagement across multiple days, enabling users to monitor fluctuations in audience interaction and identify peak engagement periods.


## 💬 Sentiment Trend Analysis

A trend line compares the proportions of:

- Positive Sentiment
- Neutral Sentiment
- Negative Sentiment

across two reporting periods, helping evaluate changes in audience perception over time.


## 📆 Weekly Performance Comparison

A clustered column chart displays engagement by day of the week, allowing users to identify the best-performing days for content publishing.


## 📱 Platform Percentage Contribution

A bar chart compares the percentage contribution of each platform, providing insight into the relative performance of different social media channels.


# 🔍 Key Insights

Based on the dashboard, several business insights can be derived:

- Engagement levels vary significantly across social media platforms.
- Some platforms generate substantially higher virality than others.
- Audience sentiment is predominantly neutral to positive.
- Platform performance changes between reporting years highlight evolving audience behavior.
- Certain weekdays consistently achieve stronger engagement, providing guidance for content scheduling.
- Social media conversations differ across platforms, indicating varying audience participation levels.


